# Written by `kdos-firewall` through kdos-powerd. Edit by hand if you like —
# the surface rewrites the whole file from the rules it finds here, so a rule
# it does not recognise is DROPPED on the next toggle. Put anything hand-made
# in a file of your own beside this one; every *.nft here is included.
#
# NAMED SERVICES ONLY, and the names live in kdos-powerd rather than here: a
# client that could name a port could open any port, and the point of the
# surface is that it cannot. `kdos-power firewall list` prints the table.
#
# Rules are added to the existing input chain — no `type`/`hook` line, which
# is what re-opens a chain rather than declaring a second one.

table inet filter {
	chain input {
	}
}
